<p>The Forward Euler algorithm can yield inaccurate results unless</p>
 <answer name="ans2a">
   <choice credit="1">the algorithm is implemented over many small time steps with a computer program.</choice>
   <choice>you always keep at least 7 decimal places when calculating subsequent time steps.</choice>
   <choice>you always work with fractions rather than decimals in intermediate steps.</choice>
   <choice>the differential equation is a polynomial function of degree 2 or greater.</choice>
 </answer>
<hint>See <ref to="$v1">Key Moment 2</ref></hint>
</exercise>
</problem>

  
